      "answer": "$2x-2y+z=9$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "EITHER use scalar products to obtain a relevant equation in $a,b,c$, e.g. $-a+b+4c=0$ - B1; obtain a second equation, e.g. $2a+b-2c=0$, and solve for one ratio, e.g. $a:b$ - M1; obtain $a:b:c=2:-2:1$, or equivalent - A1; substitute $(3,-2,-1)$ and the values of $a,b,c$ in the general equation and find $d$ - M1; obtain $2x-2y+z=9$, or equivalent - A1. OR1 attempt to calculate $(-\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}+4\\mathbf{k})\\times(2\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}-2\\mathbf{k})$ - (M1; obtain two correct components - A1; obtain a correct answer, e.g. $-6\\mathbf{i}+6\\mathbf{j}-3\\mathbf{k}$ - A1; substitute $(3,-2,-1)$ in $-6x+6y-3z=d$, or equivalent, and find $d$ - M1; obtain $-2x+2y-z=-9$, or equivalent - A1). OR2 form a two-parameter equation for the plane using the relevant point and vectors - (M1; state a correct equation, e.g. $\\mathbf{r}=3\\mathbf{i}-2\\mathbf{j}-\\mathbf{k}+\\lambda(-\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}+4\\mathbf{k})+\\mu(2\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}-2\\mathbf{k})$ - A1; state three correct equations in $x,y,z,\\lambda,\\mu$ - A1; eliminate $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$ - M1; obtain $2x-2y+z=9$, or equivalent - A1). OR3 form a determinant equation for the plane using the relevant point and vectors - (M1; state $\\begin{vmatrix}x-3&y+2&z+1\\\\-1&1&4\\\\2&1&-2\\end{vmatrix}=0$ - A1; attempt to expand the determinant - M1; obtain two correct cofactors - A1; obtain $-2x+2y-z=-9$, or equivalent - A1). Total: 5.",
